INT. DRIVE-THROUGH PET CREMATORIUM - DAY

A cheerful pastel lobby with a bell on the counter and a drive-up window. A framed poster reads "FOREVER FRIENDS."

NORBERT FENWICK, 50s, in a lanyard, sits peacefully with a mug of tea and a crossword.

An INTERCOM crackles on the wall.

INTERCOM VOICE (V.O.)
Hello? I'd like to drop off my hamster.

NORBERT
Of course. Pull up to the window and we'll take care of everything.

INTERCOM VOICE (V.O.)
He's very special.

NORBERT
They always are.

INTERCOM VOICE (V.O.)
He's, um, a big hamster.

NORBERT
(into intercom)
Sir, we do all sizes.

The door bursts open. CASSIUS OYELARAN, 40s, a rancher's hat and a wheelbarrow, rolls in a limp, truck-sized capybara draped in a bedsheet.

CASSIUS
I couldn't wait in the line.

Norbert sets down his tea. He stares at the wheelbarrow. He stares at the intercom.

NORBERT
Then who's on the intercom?

The intercom crackles.

INTERCOM VOICE (V.O.)
That would be his wife.
